            <div xml:id="d796">

                <pb facs="0821" n="813" sameAs="frus:frus1939v02/pg813"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">852.2221/1704a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Spain</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Weddell</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1939-07-26T19:00:00-04:00">July 26, 1939—7 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>63. Your 136, July 25, 3 p.m.,<anchor n="92" xml:id="d796-f1"/> last paragraph.
                    David McKelvey White, National Chairman of the Friends of the Abraham Lincoln
                    Brigade in New York, has advised Department that he hopes to be able within 2 or
                    3 days to deposit sufficient funds with Department to cover cost of repatriation
                    of volunteers who may be released by Spanish authorities. Upon receipt of funds
                    you will be advised and Embassy in Paris will be authorized to draw drafts and
                    make necessary arrangements for transportation of men from frontier at
                    Hendaye.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
